cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its methods, please cite it as below."
title: "conformal-selective-uq: a pre-registered study of selective conformal regression under distribution shift"
abstract: >-
  Selective conformal regression checked against a known noise floor. The
  demonstration task is a semi-synthetic portfolio-allocation problem on public
  US equity data. Each stock's weight mixes a part the public features can
  recover with a hidden component the model never sees, so the unrecoverable
  share is known for every stock. On this testbed the abstention score finds the
  noisy stocks (AUC 0.81), and online conformal recovers most of the
  worst-group coverage a regime shift removes (0.51 to 0.82, target 0.90). Every
  experiment froze its decision rule before running, and every verdict is
  reported as pre-registered, including the checks that failed.
type: software
